                <pb facs="1302" n="1144" sameAs="frus:frus1906p2/pg1144"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to Ambassador
                        Thompson</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-04-09"><hi rendition="#italic">April 9,
                        1906</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Your No. 13. Gist of instruction No. 103 should be made known to minister foreign
                    affairs in course of conversation at some convenient opportunity.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bacon.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
